{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":9454,"name":"Johnny Wyles","username":"JohnnyWyles","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.osmosis.zone/johnnywyles/{size}/3114_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-15T17:02:34.757Z","cooked":"\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBackbone’s bOSMO staking contract has a defect that pays out about 50% more OSMO than it should on every redemption.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe community pool held about 97% of all bOSMO. To recover it without letting the defect take OSMO from other holders, almost all of the OSMO in the contract was redeemed in a single transaction on 10 October.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery other bOSMO holder at that moment is being compensated in full, at the contract’s own redemption rate from just before the redemption: 1.1174 OSMO per bOSMO. That’s about 40,508 OSMO across 1,037 accounts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou don’t need to do anything. Payments are sent automatically after the redeemed OSMO arrives on 24 October.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebOSMO now has very little backing. Please don’t buy bOSMO or provide liquidity in bOSMO pools.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-what-happened-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-what-happened-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat happened\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebOSMO is Backbone Labs’ liquid staking token for OSMO. Its staking contract holds staked OSMO and is meant to pay each redeeming holder their share at the current redemption rate, about 1.117 OSMO per bOSMO.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile preparing the community pool’s redemption, we found that every redemption since at least April 2026 has paid about 1.676 OSMO per bOSMO instead. The extra OSMO comes out of the backing for everyone else’s bOSMO, so each redemption quietly left the remaining holders with less.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe cause is a bug in the staking contract’s code. When it calculates how much to pay, it counts the OSMO staked with Backbone’s own validator twice. A newer version of the contract code fixes it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-how-the-community-pools-bosmo-was-redeemed-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-how-the-community-pools-bosmo-was-redeemed-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow the community pool’s bOSMO was redeemed\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGovernance approved withdrawing the community pool’s Margined vault positions and burning the recovered OSMO in\u003ca href=\"https://daodao.zone/dao/osmosis/proposals/1049\"\u003e Proposal 1049\u003c/a\u003e. One of those vaults held about 1,137,000 bOSMO, roughly 97% of the supply.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause of the defect, there were only two options:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRedeem the community pool’s bOSMO in small amounts. Each redemption would have been overpaid at the expense of the other holders.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRedeem in one go, and compensate the other holders directly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe second option was the only one that treats every holder fairly. On 10 October, 776,000 bOSMO was redeemed in one transaction, which draws about 1,299,687 OSMO, almost all of the OSMO in the contract. That OSMO finishes unbonding on 24 October.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-compensation-for-bosmo-holders-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-compensation-for-bosmo-holders-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCompensation for bOSMO holders\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery account that held bOSMO at block 72,237,940 (10 October 2026, 02:59 BST), the block the redemption ran, is paid the value of its bOSMO at \u003cstrong\u003e1.1174 OSMO per bOSMO\u003c/strong\u003e. That’s the contract’s own redemption rate just before the redemption, so holders receive what their bOSMO was worth before anything changed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbout 40,508 OSMO goes to 1,037 accounts.\u003c/strong\u003e It will be sent directly to your wallet once unbonding completes on 24 October.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ebOSMO held inside contracts is paid to the people behind it,\u003c/strong\u003e read from each contract’s records at the snapshot block:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eliquidity providers in the bOSMO pools;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNecropolis marketplace users with open offers or unclaimed proceeds, and sellers whose listed NFTs received bOSMO airdrops;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGalactic Mining Club stakers with unclaimed rewards;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eholders of the FractalFun fMAD vault;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eaccounts with open orders.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAccounts worth less than 1 OSMO in total aren’t paid,\u003c/strong\u003e because a payment would cost about as much as it’s worth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe community pool’s own bOSMO isn’t compensated.\u003c/strong\u003e Its value comes back through the redemption. The community pool has not lost OSMO on this deployment, but has also not met the expected gains from staking and trading.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAccounts that took advantage of the defect after the redemption are excluded.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBackbone Labs’ own bOSMO isn’t compensated.\u003c/strong\u003e Its share, about 2,787 OSMO, goes toward reimbursing the sellers of NFTs bought on Necropolis (below).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe full recipient list and the excluded list are linked below. If you held bOSMO at the snapshot and can’t find your address, or think your amount is wrong, reply in this thread with your address, and we’ll check it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-if-you-still-hold-bosmo-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-if-you-still-hold-bosmo-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you still hold bOSMO\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYour compensation is fixed to your balance at the snapshot.\u003c/strong\u003e Selling, redeeming or transferring bOSMO afterwards doesn’t change it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYour remaining bOSMO is now worth very little.\u003c/strong\u003e Redeeming it through Backbone returns roughly 0.06 OSMO per bOSMO. Whether you redeem it or hold it is up to you.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ebOSMO bought after the snapshot is not compensated.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-please-avoid-bosmo-and-bosmo-pools-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-please-avoid-bosmo-and-bosmo-pools-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlease avoid bOSMO and bOSMO pools\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUntil the contract is updated, the defect still applies, and anyone can still mint new bOSMO at about 0.039 OSMO each. Some bOSMO pools still price bOSMO well above what it can now be redeemed for, and liquidity in them can be drained by trading against that gap. \u003cstrong\u003eIf you provide liquidity in a pool that contains bOSMO, we recommend withdrawing it.\u003c/strong\u003e We also recommend not buying bOSMO.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe’ve told Backbone about the defect and the fix, and are working with them on it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-nfts-sold-on-necropolis-for-bosmo-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-nfts-sold-on-necropolis-for-bosmo-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNFTs sold on Necropolis for bOSMO\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNecropolis prices every listing in bOSMO. Listings made before the redemption still asked the same number of bOSMO, which could now be minted for a small fraction of what it was worth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOn 13 and 14 October, one account bought 27 NFTs this way:\u003c/strong\u003e 6 Mad Scientists and 21 Galactic Mining Club. They were listed at 62,571 bOSMO, about 69,920 OSMO at the old rate, and the buyer spent about 2,519 OSMO.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNecropolis was frozen on 15 October at 02:32 BST,\u003c/strong\u003e so no more listings can be bought. Cancelling a listing still works while it is frozen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf you have NFTs listed for bOSMO,\u003c/strong\u003e you can still cancel your listing; otherwise, all bOSMO listings will be cancelled automatically soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThese sales happened after the snapshot, so the compensation above doesn’t cover them.\u003c/strong\u003e We’re looking at what can be done for the sellers and will update this thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-what-happens-next-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-what-happens-next-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat happens next\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e24 October:\u003c/strong\u003e the redeemed OSMO finishes unbonding and is withdrawn.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eShortly after:\u003c/strong\u003e the compensation payments are sent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThen:\u003c/strong\u003e the rest of the recovered OSMO is burned, as \u003ca href=\"https://daodao.zone/dao/osmosis/proposals/1049\"\u003eProposal 1049\u003c/a\u003e set out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe’ll post here when the payments are sent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-9454-provisional-recipient-listhttpsdrivegooglecomfiled1g8qgrholeua3rzxa9lhywdly5lf5dt6cviewuspsharing-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-9454-provisional-recipient-listhttpsdrivegooglecomfiled1g8qgrholeua3rzxa9lhywdly5lf5dt6cviewuspsharing-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G8qGRHOLeUa3RZxa9LHYWdLy5LF5dt6c/view?usp=sharing\"\u003eProvisional Recipient List\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-10-15T17:02:34.757Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":95,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":185.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":4161,"topic_slug":"bosmo-redemption-issue","display_username":"Johnny Wyles","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://daodao.zone/dao/osmosis/proposals/1049","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"DAO DAO","clicks":3},{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G8